*   Skilled workforce: Poland has a developed and mature market for shared services, with highly skilled specialists in accounting, HR, and customer service. The workforce also has strong language skills, including niche languages.
*   Cost-effectiveness: Employment costs in Poland are significantly lower than in many other European countries, making it an appealing option for companies looking for cost savings without compromising on quality.

## What would be three pieces of advice you would give to an investor who wants to start up a service/BPO centre in your country?

