Despite the unstable economic and political situation, the Business Services sector in Poland is expected to continue its rapid development and create high-tech jobs. Stable forecasts predict a growth rate of around 4% in 2023. The increasing pace of technological change, accelerated by the pandemic, has created a higher demand for specialists with expertise in areas such as cloud architecture, Big Data, process automation, and cybersecurity. Digital skills are also becoming increasingly necessary in other industries, including marketing, sales, logistics, finance, and accounting.

